WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.020 --> 00:00:04.880
I'm Jenna Fisher.
我是珍娜·费舍尔。

2
00:00:04.900 --> 00:00:06.300
And I'm Angela Kinsey.
我是安吉拉·金赛。

3
00:00:06.480 --> 00:00:09.160
We were on The Office together, and we're best friends.
我们曾一起出演《办公室》，而且我们是最好的朋友。

4
00:00:09.380 --> 00:00:13.280
And now we're doing the ultimate Office Lovers podcast just for you.
现在，我们专门为你带来了终极的《办公室》粉丝播客。

5
00:00:13.600 --> 00:00:17.780
Each week, we will dive deeper into the world of The Office with exclusive interviews,
每周，我们都会通过独家采访深入探索《办公室》的世界，

6
00:00:18.040 --> 00:00:20.920
behind-the-scenes details, and lots of BFF stories.
分享幕后细节，还有许多我们闺蜜之间的故事。

7
00:00:21.040 --> 00:00:23.000
We're The Office Lady 6.0.
我们是《办公室女士》6.0版。

8
00:00:25.470 --> 00:00:25.990
Hello.
你好。

9
00:00:26.430 --> 00:00:27.150
Hey there.
嘿。

10
00:00:27.550 --> 00:00:29.890
I'm very excited about today's episode.
我对今天的节目感到非常兴奋。

11
00:00:30.310 --> 00:00:31.190
Same lady.
我也是，亲爱的。

12
00:00:31.490 --> 00:00:34.770
We have been wanting to have this guest on for a long time,
我们一直很想邀请这位嘉宾来做客，

13
00:00:34.770 --> 00:00:36.270
and it finally happened.
现在终于实现了。

14
00:00:36.930 --> 00:00:39.410
Jenna, you want to tell everyone who we're talking to today?
珍娜，你想告诉大家我们今天采访的是谁吗？

15
00:00:40.070 --> 00:00:41.450
Well, yes.
好的，没问题。

16
00:00:41.650 --> 00:00:44.710
We are talking with Tig Notaro.
我们今天采访的是蒂格·诺塔罗。

17
00:00:45.250 --> 00:00:48.250
Remember when we broke down Test the Store in Season 8?
还记得我们解析第八季《测试商店》那一集的时候吗？

18
00:00:48.630 --> 00:00:50.530
We were not able to speak with her.
当时我们没能采访到她。

19
00:00:50.650 --> 00:00:52.250
And we got a lot of mail.
结果我们收到了很多来信。

20
00:00:52.450 --> 00:00:52.790
Yeah.
没错。

21
00:00:52.790 --> 00:00:53.790
I want to read you some.
我想读几封给你听听。

22
00:00:54.350 --> 00:00:55.210
Kimberly T.
来自犹他州的金伯利·T说，

23
00:00:55.430 --> 00:00:56.290
from Utah said,
“求求你们，一定要采访蒂格·诺塔罗。”

24
00:00:56.430 --> 00:00:59.270
Please, please interview Tig Notaro for this episode.
“你们的播客和她的播客是我最喜欢的两个，我太期待看到你们联动了。”

25
00:00:59.450 --> 00:01:03.910
Your podcast and hers are two of my favorites, and I'm dying for a crossover.
还有来自波士顿的阿比盖尔·D说，

26
00:01:03.910 --> 00:01:05.650
And Abigail D.
“特别嘉宾预警。”

27
00:01:05.790 --> 00:01:06.650
from Boston said,
“我超级喜欢情景喜剧女王蒂格·诺塔罗，她在剧中饰演蒂凡尼的妈妈。”

28
00:01:07.030 --> 00:01:08.050
Special guest star alert.
“她还出演过《杰茜驾到》、《速成家庭》、《废柴联盟》和《初来乍到》。”

29
00:01:08.290 --> 00:01:12.870
I absolutely love the sitcom queen Tig Notaro as Tiffany's mom.
“她是一位非常有才华的单口喜剧演员，看到她在剧中有这么出色的表现，我真是太开心了。”

30
00:01:13.210 --> 00:01:17.950
She's also been in episodes of New Girl, Instant Family, Community, and Fresh Off the Boat.
“干得好，蒂格。”

31
00:01:18.170 --> 00:01:23.890
Such a talented stand-up comedian, and I was just so tickled to see her do such a great job on this show.
其实，当蒂格在拍摄现场时，我们都非常兴奋。

32
00:01:24.190 --> 00:01:25.310
Way to go, Tig.
我们很高兴她能成为《办公室》的一员。

33
00:01:25.310 --> 00:01:30.250
Well, we were so excited when Tig was on set when we filmed this.
我们一直是她的忠实粉丝。

34
00:01:30.470 --> 00:01:32.450
We were thrilled she was going to be part of The Office.
现在依然是。

35
00:01:32.470 --> 00:01:34.130
We were big fans.
正如阿比盖尔所说，蒂格是一位单口喜剧演员。

36
00:01:34.270 --> 00:01:35.270
We're still big fans.
她还是一位演员、编剧、制片人和播客主持人。

37
00:01:35.410 --> 00:01:38.750
And as Abigail said, Tig is a stand-up comedian.
她的专辑《Live》曾获得格莱美奖提名。

38
00:01:39.110 --> 00:01:42.730
She's an actress, a writer, producer, podcaster.
她的特别节目《男孩气的女孩被打断》获得了艾美奖和格莱美奖提名。

39
00:01:42.990 --> 00:01:46.490
She's been nominated for a Grammy Award for her album Live.
她创作过多个单口喜剧专场，是深夜脱口秀节目的常客，

40
00:01:46.490 --> 00:01:52.230
And her special, Boyish Girl Interrupted, was nominated for an Emmy Award and a Grammy.
你可以在许多电视节目和电影中看到她的身影。

41
00:01:52.570 --> 00:01:57.070
She has written several stand-up specials, is a favorite on late-night talk shows,
最近，你可以观看她的新喜剧专场《Hello Again》，

42
00:01:57.170 --> 00:02:00.730
and you can see her in many television shows and filMs.
该片由她的妻子斯蒂芬妮·艾伦执导。

43
00:02:00.970 --> 00:02:05.290
Most recently, you can catch her on her new comedy special, Hello Again,
她还出演了《早间新闻》和《星际迷航：发现号》，

44
00:02:05.510 --> 00:02:07.990
that was directed by her wife, Stephanie Allen.
目前正在拍摄《星际迷航》的《星际舰队学院》系列剧。

45
00:02:07.990 --> 00:02:11.230
And she's on the morning show, Star Trek Discovery,
安吉，你问了她很多关于这方面的问题。

46
00:02:11.470 --> 00:02:15.250
and she is filming Star Trek's Starfleet Academy series now.
确实问了。

47
00:02:15.690 --> 00:02:17.770
You asked her a lot about it, Ange.
安吉拉真的对……非常着迷。

48
00:02:17.830 --> 00:02:18.150
I did.
我是说，能参与这样一部重量级的大制作，真的很了不起。

49
00:02:18.150 --> 00:02:20.230
Angela really geeked out on the...
没错，这真的是一部非常非常棒的剧集。

50
00:02:20.230 --> 00:02:24.930
I mean, this is a huge, huge show to be a part of.
确实如此。

51
00:02:25.030 --> 00:02:25.770
It's a big deal.
这可是件大事。

52
00:02:25.910 --> 00:02:27.930
And we also got a lot of mail from you all about it.
我们也收到了很多你们关于此事的来信。

53
00:02:27.930 --> 00:02:28.190
Yeah.
没错。

54
00:02:28.670 --> 00:02:31.810
She was also in Justin Noble and Mindy Kaling's show,
她还出演了贾斯汀·诺布尔和敏迪·卡灵的剧集，

55
00:02:31.910 --> 00:02:33.950
Sex Lives of College Girls on Netflix.
Netflix上的《大学女生的性生活》。

56
00:02:34.290 --> 00:02:36.550
Well, Mindy is a very big fan of Tig.
嗯，敏迪是蒂格的超级粉丝。

57
00:02:36.550 --> 00:02:42.750
We shared when we broke down Test the Store that it was Mindy who requested Tig for the role of Tiffany's mom.
我们在拆解《商店测试》那一集时分享过，是敏迪钦点蒂格出演蒂芬妮的妈妈。

58
00:02:43.070 --> 00:02:43.290
Yeah.
没错。

59
00:02:43.550 --> 00:02:47.630
And I went back and re-watched Test the Store's superfan episode on Peacock.
我回去重温了Peacock上《商店测试》的超级粉丝那一集。

60
00:02:47.690 --> 00:02:47.910
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

61
00:02:48.230 --> 00:02:51.910
Tig's scene has an extra couplet of dialogue, and it cracked me up.
蒂格的那场戏多了一句对白，把我逗乐了。

62
00:02:51.990 --> 00:02:52.970
I thought we should hear it.
我觉得我们应该听听看。

63
00:02:54.210 --> 00:02:57.310
Now, if your attacker is willing to defile a corpse,
听着，如果袭击你的人打算亵渎尸体，

64
00:02:57.370 --> 00:03:01.450
you better stop playing dead right away and just make it known that you're alive.
你最好立刻停止装死，直接表明你还活着。

65
00:03:01.690 --> 00:03:02.870
Forgive me for interrupting.
抱歉打断一下。

66
00:03:02.870 --> 00:03:06.570
I believe my daughter had an altercation with somebody here.
我想我女儿在这里和某人发生了争执。

67
00:03:06.750 --> 00:03:09.210
Some fancy gentleman with a squeaky voice?
是不是有个声音尖细的讲究绅士？

68
00:03:09.210 --> 00:03:11.210
I think you guys might have the wrong office.
我想你们可能找错办公室了。

69
00:03:11.490 --> 00:03:12.150
That's him.
就是他。

70
00:03:12.470 --> 00:03:13.370
The guy I hit.
我打的那个人。

71
00:03:13.470 --> 00:03:13.730
What?
什么？

72
00:03:14.550 --> 00:03:15.030
What?
什么？

73
00:03:15.170 --> 00:03:16.030
You've got to be kidding me.
你一定是在开玩笑。

74
00:03:16.330 --> 00:03:17.430
Poor Andy.
可怜的安迪。

75
00:03:18.390 --> 00:03:21.850
First you got beat up by a gang, and now she kicks your ass?
先是被一群人揍了一顿，现在又被她打了一顿？

76
00:03:22.130 --> 00:03:22.180
No, Kevin.
不，凯文。

77
00:03:22.590 --> 00:03:24.590
What about the lady you hit with a pine cone?
那你用松果砸的那位女士呢？

78
00:03:25.030 --> 00:03:25.430
There.
在那儿。

79
00:03:25.670 --> 00:03:26.430
That chubby one.
那个胖乎乎的。

80
00:03:27.470 --> 00:03:28.890
I just had a baby.
我刚生完孩子。

81
00:03:29.350 --> 00:03:29.830
Yesterday.
就在昨天。

82
00:03:30.350 --> 00:03:30.750
Wow.
哇。

83
00:03:31.570 --> 00:03:32.050
Apologize.
道歉。

84
00:03:32.670 --> 00:03:35.630
Sorry I kicked your ass in front of your thin girlfriend.
抱歉我在你苗条的女友面前把你揍了一顿。

85
00:03:35.990 --> 00:03:38.030
How about we wait till next year after you have your kid?
我们要不要等到明年你生完孩子再说？

86
00:03:38.650 --> 00:03:39.190
You know what?
你知道吗？

87
00:03:39.350 --> 00:03:40.510
Tiffy's going to college.
蒂菲要去上大学了。

88
00:03:40.750 --> 00:03:42.990
Listen, I don't know what you guys are talking about,
听着，我不知道你们在说什么，

89
00:03:43.050 --> 00:03:46.650
but I guess I'll just accept your apology so we can get on with our day.
但我猜我还是接受你们的道歉吧，这样我们就能继续过我们的一天了。

90
00:03:47.570 --> 00:03:48.710
Sorry I punched you.
抱歉我打了你。

91
00:03:49.810 --> 00:03:51.990
And I promise I'll take it off Facebook.
我保证会把它从Facebook上删掉。

92
00:03:52.370 --> 00:03:53.070
It's on Facebook.
它在Facebook上呢。

93
00:03:53.730 --> 00:03:54.610
There we go.
这就对了。

94
00:03:55.890 --> 00:03:56.670
God bless.
上帝保佑。

95
00:03:56.670 --> 00:03:58.990
A friend of mine uses your paper.
我的一个朋友用你们的纸。

96
00:03:59.270 --> 00:04:00.290
You do good work.
你们做得很好。

97
00:04:01.210 --> 00:04:01.930
Bye-bye.
再见。

98
00:04:02.150 --> 00:04:02.450
Bye.
再见。

99
00:04:05.390 --> 00:04:10.670
I'm so glad you played that, Angela, because, well, you'll hear in the interview,
安吉拉，我很高兴你放了这段，因为，嗯，你会在采访中听到，

100
00:04:10.970 --> 00:04:16.630
but Tig has a very unique point of view of shooting that scene that is so funny.
但蒂格对拍摄那场戏有着非常独特的视角，真的太搞笑了。

101
00:04:16.730 --> 00:04:17.010
Yes.
是的。

102
00:04:17.130 --> 00:04:22.750
Her memory of filming it is hilarious, and it's a piece of information neither of us knew.
她对拍摄那段经历的记忆太搞笑了，而且那是我们俩都不知道的信息。

103
00:04:23.030 --> 00:04:24.270
She's never shared it before.
她以前从未分享过。

104
00:04:24.810 --> 00:04:30.110
But I loved the extra couplet of dialogue about the fact that her daughter had uploaded it to Facebook.
但我很喜欢那句关于她女儿把它传到脸书上的额外对话。

105
00:04:30.430 --> 00:04:30.690
Yes.
没错。

106
00:04:30.970 --> 00:04:32.710
Further humiliation for Andy.
安迪又多了一层羞辱。

107
00:04:32.990 --> 00:04:33.390
Yes.
是的。

108
00:04:33.970 --> 00:04:36.190
Well, everyone, why don't we take a break?
好了，各位，我们休息一下好吗？

109
00:04:36.330 --> 00:04:37.670
Why wait any longer?
何必再等呢？

110
00:04:37.850 --> 00:04:40.390
And then when we come back, it's our interview with Tig Notaro.
等我们回来，就是对蒂格·诺塔罗的采访了。

111
00:04:40.590 --> 00:04:41.710
Yeah, let's do it.
好，就这么办。

112
00:04:48.600 --> 00:04:51.880
Attention all new and existing members of the WDNC.
请注意，所有WDNC的新老成员。

113
00:04:52.120 --> 00:04:55.740
I'm Melanie Sanders, and this is the We Do Not Care Club podcaSt.
我是梅兰妮·桑德斯，这是“我们不在乎俱乐部”播客。

114
00:04:56.160 --> 00:04:59.980
We got to midlife and realized we just simply do not care much anymore.
我们到了中年，意识到我们真的没那么在乎了。

115
00:04:59.980 --> 00:05:08.040
Now, we got to help each other make sense of hot flashes, itchy ears, chin hair, trifling families, brain fog, and bat wings.
现在，我们要互相帮助，去理解潮热、耳朵发痒、下巴长毛、琐碎的家庭、脑雾和蝴蝶袖。

116
00:05:08.280 --> 00:05:10.920
We are not alone, and we will be heard.
我们并不孤单，我们的声音会被听到。

117
00:05:11.100 --> 00:05:12.820
So come join the WDNC.
所以快来加入WDNC吧。

118
00:05:13.060 --> 00:05:18.380
Follow and listen to the We Do Not Care Club podcast with Melanie Sanders wherever you get your podcasts.
在任何收听播客的地方，关注并收听梅兰妮·桑德斯的“我们不在乎俱乐部”播客。

119
00:05:19.380 --> 00:05:23.160
Hello there.
你好。

120
00:05:23.940 --> 00:05:25.060
Are you talking to me?
你在跟我说话吗？

121
00:05:25.280 --> 00:05:26.020
We are.
是的。

122
00:05:26.040 --> 00:05:26.600
Oh, okay.
哦，好的。

123
00:05:26.760 --> 00:05:31.260
I wasn't sure if, like, you needed to do a little something and then talk to me and then.
我不确定你们是不是需要先做点什么，然后再跟我说话，或者……

124
00:05:31.360 --> 00:05:32.460
Oh, we'll do that.
哦，我们会做的。

125
00:05:32.460 --> 00:05:34.220
But we don't make you sit through it.
但我们不会让你干坐着等。

126
00:05:34.500 --> 00:05:34.900
Okay.
好的。

127
00:05:35.020 --> 00:05:37.280
We're like, hey, we've got a great episode for you today.
我们就像是，嘿，今天我们有一期很棒的节目。

128
00:05:37.620 --> 00:05:38.520
Tig is here.
蒂格来了。

129
00:05:38.520 --> 00:05:39.380
We did that already.
我们已经做过那个了。

130
00:05:39.540 --> 00:05:39.680
Yeah.
是啊。

131
00:05:39.860 --> 00:05:39.980
Okay.
好吧。

132
00:05:40.160 --> 00:05:41.920
But we're super excited to see you.
但我们真的超级兴奋能见到你。

133
00:05:42.060 --> 00:05:44.040
I am very excited to be here.
我也非常高兴能来到这里。

134
00:05:44.380 --> 00:05:49.740
Tig, we asked our listeners to send in questions for you, and we're going to ask you some of their questions.
蒂格，我们让听众给你发来了问题，我们要问你其中一些。

135
00:05:49.940 --> 00:05:50.160
Okay.
好的。

136
00:05:50.160 --> 00:05:54.340
But I have to share that when I was going through the digital mailbag,
但我必须分享一下，当我翻看电子信箱时，

137
00:05:54.600 --> 00:06:03.320
I have not forever in the five years we've been doing this seen the kind of letters that you inspired from people.
在我们做节目的这五年里，我从未见过像你这样激发了大家写信热情的嘉宾。

138
00:06:03.320 --> 00:06:05.700
And we've talked to a lot of people, Tig.
而且我们聊过很多人了，蒂格。

139
00:06:06.040 --> 00:06:06.520
Have you?
是吗？

140
00:06:06.660 --> 00:06:06.940
Yeah.
是的。

141
00:06:07.160 --> 00:06:08.240
This isn't episode one.
这可不是第一期节目。

142
00:06:10.660 --> 00:06:12.320
It's our news pin-off podcaSt.
这是我们的新闻衍生播客。

143
00:06:12.680 --> 00:06:15.320
We got a lot of not questions for you.
我们收到了很多不是问题的问题。

144
00:06:15.460 --> 00:06:15.760
Oh.
哦。

145
00:06:15.760 --> 00:06:20.520
Just letters from people expressing their enthusiasm for you, and I'm going to read you one.
只是人们表达对你热情的信件，我要读给你听一封。

146
00:06:20.700 --> 00:06:21.720
That's so nice.
那太好了。

147
00:06:21.720 --> 00:06:23.660
I thought it would be a good way to kick things off.
我觉得这是个不错的开场方式。

148
00:06:23.740 --> 00:06:24.980
I hope it's a long letter.
希望那是一封长信。

149
00:06:25.220 --> 00:06:26.020
It's not.
并不是。

150
00:06:26.140 --> 00:06:26.360
Oh.
哦。

151
00:06:26.360 --> 00:06:27.680
It's a short one.
这篇很短。

152
00:06:27.680 --> 00:06:28.060
Okay.
好的。

153
00:06:28.340 --> 00:06:28.880
But it's great.
但很棒。

154
00:06:29.020 --> 00:06:29.800
I'll still hear it.
我还是会听的。

155
00:06:30.020 --> 00:06:31.080
It's from Rebecca D.
来自爱丁堡的

156
00:06:31.180 --> 00:06:31.680
in Edinburgh.
丽贝卡·D。

157
00:06:32.100 --> 00:06:32.600
Hi, Rebecca.
嗨，丽贝卡。

158
00:06:33.160 --> 00:06:35.160
Rebecca said, Tig, why are you so amazing?
丽贝卡说，蒂格，你为什么这么了不起？

159
00:06:35.660 --> 00:06:39.240
How do I become more like you, and where do I sign up to be your friend?
