00:19:48.280 --> 00:19:54.300
Because you're just looking at your dialogue and you'll see maybe only have seven lines
因为你只看自己的台词，你会发现也许10页里，

445
00:19:54.300 --> 00:19:55.540
in the 10 pages.
你只有7句台词。

446
00:19:55.780 --> 00:20:01.120
And it can really give you an idea like, oh, I don't need to panic because I just have these
这真的能让你意识到，哦，我不需要恐慌，因为我只需要背这，

447
00:20:01.120 --> 00:20:02.400
seven lines to learn.
7句台词。

448
00:20:02.400 --> 00:20:06.580
And then she said, just learn only your lines.
然后她说，只背你自己的台词。

449
00:20:06.960 --> 00:20:10.400
Get it to where you can say it basically like an entire monologue.
练到你可以像背独白一样顺口说出来。

450
00:20:10.660 --> 00:20:17.660
And then once you have that down, then plug it back into the script, to the sides that
一旦你掌握了这些，再把它们放回剧本里，放回那些剧本页中。

451
00:20:17.660 --> 00:20:18.100
you have.
你确实有。

452
00:20:18.100 --> 00:20:20.580
And then you're fully off book.
然后你就完全脱稿了。

453
00:20:21.460 --> 00:20:22.180
That's fantastic.
那太棒了。

454
00:20:22.240 --> 00:20:23.860
And I was like, wow.
当时我就想，哇。

455
00:20:24.060 --> 00:20:28.480
And she said, and when you've removed just your lines, you can see, oh, I do have a lot
她说，当你只留下自己的台词时，你会发现，哦，原来我有这么多

456
00:20:28.480 --> 00:20:28.960
of lines.
台词。

457
00:20:28.980 --> 00:20:31.640
Or, oh, I actually don't have that many.
或者，哦，其实我没那么多台词。

458
00:20:31.960 --> 00:20:33.760
And that helped me personally.
这对我个人很有帮助。

459
00:20:34.080 --> 00:20:34.480
Right.
没错。

460
00:20:34.540 --> 00:20:34.980
I was...
我当时……

461
00:20:34.980 --> 00:20:37.820
It's less daunting if you can just see what your part is.
如果能清楚看到自己的部分，就不会那么令人畏惧了。

462
00:20:37.820 --> 00:20:38.120
Yes.
是的。

463
00:20:38.360 --> 00:20:38.620
Yeah.
是啊。

464
00:20:38.760 --> 00:20:43.200
And it was easier for me to plug it back in after I isolated things.
而且在我把内容拆分出来后，再重新整合就容易多了。

465
00:20:44.100 --> 00:20:45.600
