644
00:27:29.760 --> 00:27:30.160
Yes.
是的。

645
00:27:30.380 --> 00:27:35.160
You even did a whole bit where you tried to get an auctioneer to train you to talk faSt.
你甚至还做过一个完整的段子，试图找一位拍卖师训练你说话快一点。

646
00:27:35.300 --> 00:27:35.480
Yeah.
是啊。

647
00:27:35.800 --> 00:27:36.240
Very funny.
非常搞笑。

648
00:27:36.940 --> 00:27:37.220
Thank you.
谢谢。

649
00:27:37.880 --> 00:27:44.440
We reached out to the director of your episode, Test the Store, Brent Forrester, and he sent
我们联系了你那一集《Test the Store》的导演Brent Forrester，他发来

650
00:27:44.440 --> 00:27:47.640
in an audio clip about what it was like directing you in the episode.
一段音频片段，讲述了在那一集中执导你是什么样的体验。

651
00:27:48.360 --> 00:27:49.720
And I want you to have a listen.
我想让你听听看。

652
00:27:50.140 --> 00:27:51.180
I'm sorry.
抱歉。

653
00:27:51.560 --> 00:27:53.020
Should we have given you a heads up?
我们是不是该提前知会你一声？

654
00:27:53.700 --> 00:27:54.740
It's hilarious.
这太搞笑了。

655
00:27:55.400 --> 00:27:56.660
Oh my gosh.
天哪。

656
00:27:56.960 --> 00:27:59.000
You probably can see where this is going.
你大概能猜到接下来要说什么了。

657
00:28:00.080 --> 00:28:04.840
For the part of the little girl's mom, Mindy always pictured Tig Notaro.
关于小女孩妈妈这个角色，明迪一直觉得蒂格·诺塔罗最合适。

658
00:28:05.020 --> 00:28:05.920
We didn't audition anybody.
我们没有面试任何人。

659
00:28:05.920 --> 00:28:08.320
We just offered it to Tig, and she was great.
我们直接向蒂格发出了邀请，她表现得非常棒。

660
00:28:08.540 --> 00:28:12.380
But at the time, I was concerned about the pacing of the scene.
但当时，我担心这场戏的节奏问题。

661
00:28:12.380 --> 00:28:17.240
And after the first take, I walked up to Tig, and I said, hey, Tig, I have a thought.
第一条拍完后，我走到蒂格身边说，嘿，蒂格，我有想法。

662
00:28:17.320 --> 00:28:21.400
And she said, you want me to talk faster?
她说，你是想让我说快点吗？

663
00:28:21.880 --> 00:28:23.460
And I said, yeah, how do you know?
我说，对，你怎么知道？

664
00:28:23.640 --> 00:28:31.080
And she said, every time they put me on camera, they tell me to talk faster.
她说，每次他们让我上镜，都会叫我快点说。

665
00:28:31.500 --> 00:28:33.320
And I said, can you talk faster?
我说，你能说快点吗？

666
00:28:33.480 --> 00:28:36.960
And she said, no, I can't.
她说，不，我做不到。

667
00:28:38.620 --> 00:28:40.180
Do you remember the 6G?
你还记得6G吗？

668
00:28:40.180 --> 00:28:44.480
I feel like it is an exchange I have on every set.
我觉得我在每个片场都会有这样的对话。

669
00:28:45.280 --> 00:28:46.400
Every set.
每个片场。

670
00:28:46.940 --> 00:28:56.000
In fact, it's gotten to the point where when a director comes towards me, I'll put my hand out and say,
事实上，现在已经到了这种地步：当导演朝我走过来时，我会伸出手说，

671
00:28:56.120 --> 00:28:59.320
before you give me any notes, just know I have no range.
在给我提建议之前，先告诉你，我没戏路可言。

672
00:28:59.680 --> 00:29:00.800
But go on.
不过你继续说。

673
00:29:01.140 --> 00:29:02.480
What were you going to say?
你刚才想说什么？

674
00:29:03.100 --> 00:29:08.700
I just, but it's always getting to that of like, okay, now let's do it faster.
我只是……但总是会变成那样，就是，好吧，现在我们快点来一遍。

675
00:29:08.700 --> 00:29:14.020
And, you know, and I try, but, you know.
而且，你知道，我试过了，但，你知道的。

676
00:29:14.300 --> 00:29:17.960
I just think the beauty in your comedy is your pacing.
我只是觉得你喜剧的魅力就在于你的节奏感。

677
00:29:18.280 --> 00:29:19.180
I just love it.
我真的很喜欢。

678
00:29:19.380 --> 00:29:25.440
And I feel like I couldn't imagine you tell a story not the way you tell it.
我觉得我无法想象你用别的方式来讲故事。

679
00:29:25.440 --> 00:29:26.000
Yeah.
是啊。

680
00:29:26.720 --> 00:29:35.020
There, it's, it's, it's, you know, there's a lot of talk about how, just the connection between music and comedy.
关于音乐和喜剧之间的联系，人们讨论得很多。

681
00:29:36.000 --> 00:29:38.640
And a lot of musicians want to be comedians.
很多音乐人想当喜剧演员。

682
00:29:38.760 --> 00:29:40.160
A lot of comedians want to be musicians.
很多喜剧演员想当音乐人。

683
00:29:40.180 --> 00:29:44.960
And so much of that, I don't know, the timing.
这其中很大一部分，我不知道，就是时机把握。

684
00:29:44.960 --> 00:29:49.220
Like, it feels like a rhythm and a song to me.
对我来说，这感觉就像节奏和歌曲一样。

685
00:29:49.440 --> 00:29:57.760
The way, like, I can't, the way I deliver my material, it's, it's not thought out.
我表达素材的方式，并不是经过深思熟虑的。

686
00:29:57.960 --> 00:30:02.680
It's just the natural beat and rhythm of the story.
那只是故事自然的节拍和韵律。

687
00:30:02.680 --> 00:30:13.640
And people have asked me, do you decide to pause there for two seconds or do you decide to, and I'm like, no, there's no thought.
人们问我，你是决定在那里停顿两秒，还是决定……我说，不，没想过。

688
00:30:13.820 --> 00:30:17.080
It's truly just how I deliver it.
这确实就是我表达的方式。

689
00:30:17.600 --> 00:30:19.100
Have you always had that cadence?
你一直都是这种语调吗？

690
00:30:19.720 --> 00:30:27.720
Um, I mean, I've always been, you know, told I was, yeah, slow and, and, and dry.
嗯，我是说，我一直被告知我说话……对，很慢，而且很冷幽默。

691
00:30:28.080 --> 00:30:37.420
And, um, but I think it's highlighted on stage in front of an audience, but it's not on purpose.
而且，嗯，我觉得在观众面前表演时会更突出，但那不是故意的。

692
00:30:37.760 --> 00:30:38.000
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

693
00:30:39.100 --> 00:30:45.900
I know just back when I did a ton of improv, you know, you would do a workshop and you would teach these young improvisers.
我知道以前我做过很多即兴表演，你知道，你会去办工作坊，教那些年轻的即兴表演者。

694
00:30:45.900 --> 00:30:53.960
And I always sort of felt bad saying this because I was like, oh, they're all here to learn, but you can't teach timing.
我总觉得说这话不太好，因为我想，哦，他们都是来学习的，但你没法教节奏感。

695
00:30:54.200 --> 00:30:54.520
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

696
00:30:54.620 --> 00:31:00.480
You can teach a lot of things, I feel like, for comedy, but timing is just something instinctual, I think, personally.
我觉得喜剧中很多东西是可以教的，但节奏感，我个人认为，是某种本能的东西。

697
00:31:00.720 --> 00:31:01.200
I do too.
我也这么认为。

698
00:31:01.440 --> 00:31:06.860
And it's, and it's a very different timing on and off stage as well.
而且台前和台下的节奏感也非常不同。

699
00:31:07.120 --> 00:31:12.940
I think that it's just highlighted a little more.
我觉得只是在台上被稍微放大了而已。

700
00:31:13.180 --> 00:31:13.580
Yeah.
是啊。

701
00:31:14.040 --> 00:31:14.360
Yeah.
是啊。

702
00:31:15.220 --> 00:31:20.200
We got a fan question from, uh, Natalie L.
我们收到了一位粉丝的提问，呃，来自波士顿的娜塔莉·L。

703
00:31:20.320 --> 00:31:20.940
in Boston.
在波士顿。

704
00:31:21.240 --> 00:31:21.800
Hey, Natalie.
嘿，娜塔莉。

705
00:31:22.600 --> 00:31:23.660
I love you, Tig.
我爱你，蒂格。

706
00:31:24.220 --> 00:31:28.800
Did you get to practice with the actress who played your daughter prior to the shoot day?
你在拍摄当天之前，有机会和饰演你女儿的演员排练过吗？

707
00:31:30.670 --> 00:31:33.870
Um, no, I did not.
嗯，没有，我没有。

708
00:31:35.530 --> 00:31:39.290
I, um, I was going to say I wish I had, but I don't even know.
我，嗯，我本来想说我希望我有，但我甚至不知道。

709
00:31:39.290 --> 00:31:40.550
Did you know she was playing your daughter?
你知道她是演你女儿吗？

710
00:31:40.730 --> 00:31:41.230
No, I'm kidding.
不，我开玩笑的。

711
00:31:43.390 --> 00:31:46.490
I honestly don't think I knew anything.
我老实说，我觉得我什么都不知道。

712
00:31:46.770 --> 00:31:47.210
Like, who's this person?
就像是，这人是谁？

713
00:31:47.250 --> 00:31:49.350
Yeah, like, why is she stealing my thunder?
是啊，就像是，她为什么要抢我的风头？

714
00:31:49.350 --> 00:31:50.470
I'm referring to her.
我指的是她。

715
00:31:50.690 --> 00:31:51.990
Get out of my scene, kid.
从我的戏份里走开，孩子。

716
00:31:52.750 --> 00:31:53.730
Um, yeah.
嗯，是啊。

717
00:31:54.030 --> 00:31:57.370
No, I didn't run it with anybody.
不，我没和任何人排练过。

718
00:31:58.110 --> 00:32:01.050
And is this upsetting to the office fans?
这对《办公室》的粉丝来说会让人心烦吗？

719
00:32:01.210 --> 00:32:03.590
If somebody is like, oh, I hadn't seen it.
如果有人说，哦，我没看过。

720
00:32:04.190 --> 00:32:05.610
Um, you know what I mean?
嗯，你知道我的意思吗？

721
00:32:05.610 --> 00:32:10.330
Like, I know there's rabid fans where they might be offended or something.
就像是，我知道有些狂热粉丝可能会觉得被冒犯之类的。

722
00:32:10.690 --> 00:32:12.430
Oh, that you hadn't seen it before?
哦，是指你之前没看过？

723
00:32:12.570 --> 00:32:12.810
No.
不是。

724
00:32:12.930 --> 00:32:13.130
Yeah.
是啊。

725
00:32:13.150 --> 00:32:15.510
No, because we've had a lot of different guest stars.
不是，因为我们有很多不同的客串明星。

726
00:32:15.670 --> 00:32:19.130
Some people were like, I was so nervous because I'd seen every episode.
有些人会说，我当时太紧张了，因为我每一集都看过。

727
00:32:19.330 --> 00:32:19.490
Yeah.
是啊。

728
00:32:19.490 --> 00:32:23.550
And then other people were like, I knew it was a big show, but I hadn't seen it yet.
然后其他人会说，我知道这是个大热剧，但我还没看过。

729
00:32:23.890 --> 00:32:23.990
Yeah.
是啊。

730
00:32:24.130 --> 00:32:24.310
Yeah.
是啊。

731
00:32:24.510 --> 00:32:27.250
No, and everyone's experience is completely different.
不，每个人的经历都完全不同。

732
00:32:27.470 --> 00:32:28.130
So, no.
所以，不会。

733
00:32:28.290 --> 00:32:29.070
You will not offend anybody.
你不会冒犯任何人的。

734
00:32:29.070 --> 00:32:29.670
You'll be fine.
你会没事的。

735
00:32:29.830 --> 00:32:35.970
But I do, I want to mention again that I have seen many episodes of The Office.
但我确实，我想再次提一下，我已经看过很多集《办公室》了。

736
00:32:36.190 --> 00:32:36.510
Yes.
是的。

737
00:32:36.670 --> 00:32:42.190
Because we were just blown away that our, um, our four-year-olds were just, like, so into it.
因为我们当时非常震惊，我们的，嗯，我们的四岁孩子竟然，那么喜欢它。

738
00:32:42.230 --> 00:32:44.330
Did they have a character that they were most like?
他们有最像的角色吗？

739
00:32:44.430 --> 00:32:45.710
A lot of little kids like Dwight.
很多小孩子喜欢德怀特。

740
00:32:45.850 --> 00:32:47.130
Yeah, I was going to guess Dwight.
是啊，我本来想猜德怀特。

741
00:32:47.290 --> 00:32:47.490
Yeah.
是啊。

742
00:32:47.610 --> 00:32:48.150
It was Dwight.
就是德怀特。

743
00:32:48.310 --> 00:32:48.570
Yeah.
是啊。

744
00:32:48.570 --> 00:32:48.990
Yeah.
是啊。

745
00:32:49.310 --> 00:32:50.330
And I know who Dwight is.
而且我知道德怀特是谁。

746
00:32:50.570 --> 00:32:51.050
Rain.
雷恩。

747
00:32:51.270 --> 00:32:53.790
You're not just, you're not just saying, sure, sure, yeah.
你不是，你不是只是在说，当然，当然，是啊。

748
00:32:53.950 --> 00:32:54.470
Yeah, yeah, yeah.
是啊，是啊，是啊。

749
00:32:54.670 --> 00:32:55.490
No, for sure.
不，当然。

750
00:32:55.650 --> 00:32:56.050
For sure.
当然。

751
00:32:56.490 --> 00:32:58.890
We also have this question from Colton S.
我们还有来自俄亥俄州文森特的Colton S.提出的这个问题。

752
00:32:59.070 --> 00:33:00.190
in Vincent, Ohio.
俄亥俄州文森特。

753
00:33:00.570 --> 00:33:01.510
Hey, Colton S.
嘿，Colton S.

754
00:33:01.690 --> 00:33:02.410
Colton S.
Colton S.

755
00:33:02.690 --> 00:33:04.930
says, did you break at all during the scene?
问，在拍摄那场戏时你有笑场吗？

756
00:33:05.170 --> 00:33:06.030
Did you crack up?
你有忍不住笑出来吗？

757
00:33:06.530 --> 00:33:08.110
If so, who made you break?
如果有的话，是谁让你笑场的？

758
00:33:08.870 --> 00:33:10.190
You might not know.
你可能不知道。

759
00:33:11.630 --> 00:33:12.870
Who made you break?
是谁让你笑场的？

760
00:33:13.290 --> 00:33:14.790
You, like, describe them.
你能不能描述一下他们。

761
00:33:14.790 --> 00:33:23.470
I mean, no, I have to say, I, um, I mean, I think I, I'm always amused by Ed HelMs.
我是说，不，我得说，我，嗯，我是说，我觉得我，我总是被Ed Helms逗乐。

762
00:33:23.650 --> 00:33:23.830
Yeah.
是啊。

763
00:33:23.910 --> 00:33:24.210
Yes.
没错。

764
00:33:24.250 --> 00:33:26.150
I mean, he is such a silly man.
我是说，他真是个滑稽的人。

765
00:33:26.150 --> 00:33:33.950
And I, and I know people know that, but I think he's even sillier than, I don't know.
而且我，我知道大家都知道这一点，但我认为他比，我不知道，他比那更滑稽。

766
00:33:34.030 --> 00:33:39.590
I think once you know Ed and then you see his silliness, it's, uh, it's a tickle.
我觉得一旦你了解Ed，再看到他的滑稽劲儿，那真是，呃，那真是让人忍俊不禁。

767
00:33:40.090 --> 00:33:41.130
It's a deep tickle.
那是一种发自内心的好笑。

768
00:33:41.550 --> 00:33:41.630
Yeah.
是啊。

769
00:33:41.790 --> 00:33:46.710
Um, so I can just, I don't have a great memory, but I can just assume, I, I know he was sitting
嗯，所以我可以，我的记性不太好，但我可以推测，我，我知道他当时坐在

770
00:33:46.710 --> 00:33:47.410
in the front row.
前排。

771
00:33:49.590 --> 00:33:56.230
I'm just going to assume I was tickled, but I was more so on edge, like terribly on edge
我只能假设我被逗乐了，但我那天更多的是紧张，就像非常紧张

772
00:33:56.230 --> 00:34:00.170
that day because I really, like I said, felt caught.
因为我真的，就像我说的，感觉被抓住了。

773
00:34:00.750 --> 00:34:04.390
Did you know Ed before you shot on The Office?
你在拍摄《办公室》之前认识Ed吗？

774
00:34:04.790 --> 00:34:07.750
Yeah, not, uh, not well.
嗯，不算，呃，不算很熟。

775
00:34:08.150 --> 00:34:14.150
I think just through Largo of him doing shows there and, and I did as well.
我想只是通过Largo，他在那里表演过，我也表演过。

776
00:34:14.410 --> 00:34:15.130
You're right though.
你说得对。

777
00:34:15.210 --> 00:34:16.130
He is really silly.
他真的很滑稽。

778
00:34:16.350 --> 00:34:17.090
He's so silly.
他太滑稽了。

779
00:34:17.390 --> 00:34:22.150
We used to do the stupidest bits and I know that I could call him right now and do this
我们过去常做些最蠢的梗，我知道我现在给他打电话做这个

780
00:34:22.150 --> 00:34:23.730
stupid bit and he would do it right back.
蠢梗，他也会立刻接上。

781
00:34:23.870 --> 00:34:24.050
Yeah.
是啊。

782
00:34:24.050 --> 00:34:29.650
I told him this story one time about this girl from my hometown who, if she really liked
有一次我给他讲了个故事，关于我老家有个女孩，如果她真的很喜欢

783
00:34:29.650 --> 00:34:32.470
you, she'd be like, hey, you stupid f***ing twat.
你，她会说，嘿，你这个蠢货。

784
00:34:33.630 --> 00:34:40.030
And Ed lost his mind and still to this day, we will say that to each other.
Ed当时笑疯了，直到今天，我们还会对彼此说这句话。

785
00:34:40.910 --> 00:34:43.150
And he does it right back the same way.
而且他会用同样的方式回应我。

786
00:34:43.410 --> 00:34:44.870
And, um, I'll have to do that too.
而且，嗯，我也得那样做。

787
00:34:45.050 --> 00:34:45.750
I'm next time I see him.
下次见到他的时候。

788
00:34:45.810 --> 00:34:46.010
Oh my gosh.
天哪。

789
00:34:46.430 --> 00:34:46.790
Yes.
是的。

790
00:34:47.210 --> 00:34:48.130
But you gotta do it.
但你必须得做。

791
00:34:48.910 --> 00:34:50.770
Like I'm going down a country road.
就像我走在乡间小路上一样。

792
00:34:54.970 --> 00:35:03.770
Yeah, he's, he, I think he's, even though people know he's a comedian, um, I still think
是啊，他，他，我觉得他，尽管人们知道他是喜剧演员，嗯，我仍然认为

793
00:35:03.770 --> 00:35:09.430
he, it's surprising how silly, deeply silly that man is.
他，那个男人有多滑稽，深层的滑稽，真是令人惊讶。

794
00:35:09.550 --> 00:35:09.730
Yeah.
是啊。

795
00:35:10.330 --> 00:35:11.330
In the best way.
以最好的方式。

796
00:35:20.310 --> 00:35:26.190
Well, Ed Helms famously introduced you for your comedy set that you did that went on to
嗯，Ed Helms曾为你主持过你的喜剧专场，那场演出后来

797
00:35:26.190 --> 00:35:31.530
be nominated for a Grammy where you talked about being very recently diagnosed with breast
获得了格莱美提名，你在里面谈到了自己最近被诊断出患有乳腺

798
00:35:31.530 --> 00:35:31.990
cancer.
癌。

