I mean, William Shatner is almost 100 years old.
我是说，威廉·夏特纳都快一百岁了。

1310
00:59:27.990 --> 00:59:28.690
I think he's 95.
我想他应该95岁了。

1311
00:59:29.070 --> 00:59:31.390
And he still jets off every weekend
但他每个周末还是会飞去

1312
00:59:31.390 --> 00:59:33.130
to a convention.
参加各种漫展。

1313
00:59:33.910 --> 00:59:37.070
And, I mean, have you seen this guy talk?
而且，你看过他说话的样子吗？

1314
00:59:37.270 --> 00:59:42.930
Yes, I saw him on, I forgot, the late night talk show, but he was like doing bits and had his
看过，我忘了是在哪个深夜脱口秀上看到的，但他当时在表演段子，还讲了

1315
00:59:42.930 --> 00:59:43.150
jokes.
笑话。

1316
00:59:43.730 --> 00:59:45.630
This guy has no clue he's almost 100.
这家伙完全没意识到自己快一百岁了。

1317
00:59:45.930 --> 00:59:46.130
Yeah.
确实。

1318
00:59:46.290 --> 00:59:51.210
Like, somebody needs to tell his face this, because he's just, like, walking around like
真的，得有人提醒一下他的脸，因为他走来走去的样子

1319
00:59:51.210 --> 00:59:52.190
he's not 95.
一点都不像95岁。

1320
00:59:52.670 --> 00:59:54.090
You can take the weekend off.
你完全可以周末休息一下的。

1321
00:59:54.310 --> 00:59:54.790
Truly.
真的。

1322
00:59:55.110 --> 00:59:56.170
You can put your feet up.
你可以把脚翘起来歇歇。

1323
00:59:56.310 --> 00:59:56.650
Yeah.
是啊。

1324
00:59:56.890 --> 00:59:57.030
Yeah.
没错。

1325
00:59:57.210 --> 01:00:01.530
And then I also, I have a small part on The Morning Show.
另外，我在《早间新闻》里也有个小角色。

1326
01:00:02.270 --> 01:00:03.250
I love it.
我很喜欢。

1327
01:00:03.250 --> 01:00:09.270
And it's really fun to do just, like, a dramatic, you know.
能演一部那种戏剧性的作品，感觉真的很有趣，你知道的。

1328
01:00:09.330 --> 01:00:09.770
Yeah.
嗯。

1329
01:00:10.210 --> 01:00:10.650
Show.
剧集。

1330
01:00:10.850 --> 01:00:12.030
Fast-talking drama.
节奏很快的剧情片。

1331
01:00:12.590 --> 01:00:12.790
Yeah.
是啊。

1332
01:00:12.910 --> 01:00:17.830
And I've known so many of those cast members in so many different ways over the years.
多年来，我以各种方式认识了其中的许多演员。

1333
01:00:18.250 --> 01:00:19.770
And so that's fun, too.
所以那也很有趣。

1334
01:00:20.490 --> 01:00:27.370
Part of what I enjoy about acting is this really highlights what, how much I'm not an actor,
我喜欢表演的部分原因在于，这恰恰凸显了我有多么不像个演员，

1335
01:00:27.490 --> 01:00:30.270
but when they say cut, and then I get to talk to.
但当他们喊“卡”的时候，我就能去和人聊天了。

1336
01:00:30.510 --> 01:00:31.730
Then you get to do the chitty chat.
然后你就可以开始闲聊了。

1337
01:00:31.810 --> 01:00:33.030
Then I get to talk to my co-star.
然后我就能和我的搭档聊天了。

1338
01:00:33.030 --> 01:00:38.430
That is one of the best parts of being an actor, is just existing with all of these,
做演员最好的部分之一，就是能和这些

1339
01:00:38.430 --> 01:00:43.470
like, incredibly creative, funny, interesting people.
极具创造力、风趣且有趣的人待在一起。

1340
01:00:43.690 --> 01:00:46.170
I mean, artists and actors are interesting.
我是说，艺术家和演员都很有趣。

1341
01:00:46.490 --> 01:00:46.710
Yeah.
是啊。

1342
01:00:47.090 --> 01:00:47.350
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1343
01:00:47.510 --> 01:00:47.790
Yeah.
没错。

1344
01:00:48.070 --> 01:00:49.530
So, I don't know.
所以，我也不知道。

1345
01:00:49.730 --> 01:00:55.350
Those are the two things I'm working on these days that I'm, it's fresh in my mind, and
这些就是我最近在做的两件事，它们在我脑海里还很新鲜，而且

1346
01:00:55.350 --> 01:00:56.370
I'm enjoying them.
我很享受这些过程。

1347
01:00:56.470 --> 01:00:58.010
Those are decent, you know.
这些还不错，你知道的。

1348
01:00:58.130 --> 01:00:59.210
They're not too shabby.
相当不错了。

1349
01:00:59.250 --> 01:00:59.450
Yeah.
是啊。

1350
01:00:59.570 --> 01:01:01.690
I've really enjoyed everything.
我真的很享受这一切。

1351
01:01:01.690 --> 01:01:07.250
Like, I, you know, there's been some rotten people in the mix here and there, but in general,
怎么说呢，你知道，虽然这期间偶尔也会遇到一些糟糕的人，但总的来说，

1352
01:01:07.490 --> 01:01:09.270
I've had a really great run.
我这一路走来真的很棒。

1353
01:01:09.270 --> 01:01:11.570
Can I ask you about the watch now?
现在能问问你关于这块手表的事吗？

1354
01:01:12.210 --> 01:01:15.130
So, in your new comedy special.
在你的新喜剧特辑里。

1355
01:01:15.370 --> 01:01:16.110
Hello again.
你好啊，又见面了。

1356
01:01:16.390 --> 01:01:16.550
Yes.
是的。

1357
01:01:16.630 --> 01:01:17.750
Directed by your wife.
由你妻子执导。

1358
01:01:17.870 --> 01:01:19.130
She was nominated for an Emmy.
她还获得了艾美奖提名。

1359
01:01:19.510 --> 01:01:20.230
Stephanie Allen.
斯蒂芬妮·艾伦。

1360
01:01:20.430 --> 01:01:20.610
Yep.
没错。

1361
01:01:20.970 --> 01:01:21.510
Fantastic.
太棒了。

1362
01:01:22.130 --> 01:01:23.590
I loved your special.
我很喜欢你的特辑。

1363
01:01:23.750 --> 01:01:24.110
Thank you.
谢谢。

1364
01:01:24.110 --> 01:01:27.550
I couldn't help but notice that you have on a fantastic watch.
我忍不住注意到你戴着一块很棒的手表。

1365
01:01:27.850 --> 01:01:28.370
Thank you.
谢谢你。

1366
01:01:28.490 --> 01:01:32.810
And I asked you when you came in, I want to hear about the watch.
你刚进来时我就问过你，我想听听关于这块手表的故事。

1367
01:01:32.810 --> 01:01:35.790
And you said, there's a great story about this watch.
你说过，这块手表背后有一个很棒的故事。

1368
01:01:35.810 --> 01:01:38.010
And I'm sorry I didn't notice the watch.
很抱歉我之前没注意到这块表。

1369
01:01:38.150 --> 01:01:38.910
Oh, that's fine.
哦，没关系。

1370
01:01:39.030 --> 01:01:40.650
I thought the lighting was beautiful.
我当时觉得灯光很美。

1371
01:01:40.930 --> 01:01:41.830
Well, thank you.
好吧，谢谢你。

1372
01:01:42.810 --> 01:01:49.470
So, I was like, oh, there's a story because I was thinking how it ties in also to cancer.
所以我当时想，哦，这背后肯定有故事，因为我在想它和癌症之间有什么联系。

1373
01:01:49.850 --> 01:01:54.610
Oh, years ago, I was guest starring on the Sarah Silverman program.
哦，多年前，我曾客串过《萨拉·西尔弗曼秀》。

1374
01:01:54.710 --> 01:02:01.210
And there was an actress that came on there that I had a really fun banter with and exchange
当时有一位女演员来参加节目，我们聊得很投机，互动也非常愉快，

1375
01:02:01.210 --> 01:02:04.570
to the point where I was like, she's cute.
以至于我当时觉得，她真可爱。

1376
01:02:04.910 --> 01:02:07.530
But I was like, she's not into me.
但我又想，她肯定对我没意思。

1377
01:02:07.750 --> 01:02:08.990
So, that's fine.
所以，那也没关系。

1378
01:02:09.270 --> 01:02:11.930
She was engaged to marry this guy and whatever.
她当时已经订婚了，诸如此类的。

1379
01:02:12.290 --> 01:02:14.070
But I still thought she was so funny.
但我还是觉得她非常风趣。

1380
01:02:14.230 --> 01:02:17.970
And it was just fun every time I saw her or worked with her.
每次见到她或与她共事时，都觉得很开心。

1381
01:02:18.690 --> 01:02:19.510
Years go by.
几年过去了。

1382
01:02:19.930 --> 01:02:26.250
And then I run into her right before I'm moving to New York to work on that TV show.
后来在我搬去纽约做那个电视节目之前，我又碰到了她。

1383
01:02:26.790 --> 01:02:29.070
And I hadn't been diagnosed yet.
那时我还没被确诊。

1384
01:02:29.070 --> 01:02:31.750
But we were at a table read together.
我们当时在一起参加剧本围读。

1385
01:02:32.150 --> 01:02:38.430
A friend of ours was doing a Broadway play and wanted us to read through this script with her.
我们的一位朋友在演百老汇剧，想让我们帮她读一下剧本。

1386
01:02:38.730 --> 01:02:42.650
And afterwards, we found out we were both moving to New York at the same time.
之后我们发现，我们都要在同一时间搬去纽约。

1387
01:02:42.750 --> 01:02:45.930
Well, she was divorced now.
那时她已经离婚了。

1388
01:02:46.430 --> 01:02:48.190
And we exchanged numbers.
我们交换了电话号码。

1389
01:02:48.650 --> 01:02:53.510
And well, it turns out there was something between us.
结果，我们之间确实擦出了火花。

1390
01:02:53.630 --> 01:02:56.770
And then I was diagnosed in the middle of that.
然后就在那期间，我被确诊了。

1391
01:02:56.770 --> 01:03:04.870
And I was very insecure because I was like, oh, my gosh, I can't believe this woman that I thought was so attractive and fun.
我当时非常不安，因为我在想，天哪，真不敢相信，我一直觉得这么迷人又有趣的女人，

1392
01:03:04.870 --> 01:03:06.890
And I'm getting her attention now.
现在竟然开始关注我了。

1393
01:03:07.170 --> 01:03:09.450
And now, just buzzkill.
结果却像被泼了冷水一样。

1394
01:03:09.650 --> 01:03:11.570
I just got diagnosed with cancer.
我刚被确诊患了癌症。

1395
01:03:11.570 --> 01:03:15.990
And she was so good to me during that time and helpful.
在那段日子里，她对我非常好，给了我很多帮助。

1396
01:03:16.330 --> 01:03:18.290
And then I had my surgery.
后来我做了手术。

1397
01:03:18.450 --> 01:03:20.230
I didn't have reconstructive surgery.
我没有做重建手术。

1398
01:03:20.330 --> 01:03:24.230
And so I do still just have scars on my cheSt.
所以我的胸口依然留着伤疤。

1399
01:03:24.230 --> 01:03:29.110
And I remember also feeling very insecure about my body for a while.
我记得有一段时间，我也对自己的身体感到非常自卑。

1400
01:03:29.430 --> 01:03:35.450
And when I talked to her about that, she was like, I love scars.
当我跟她谈起这件事时，她说，我喜欢伤疤。

1401
01:03:36.030 --> 01:03:38.650
I think scars are so hot and sexy.
我觉得伤疤特别性感迷人。

1402
01:03:38.770 --> 01:03:40.350
And I was like, what?
当时我就想，什么？

1403
01:03:40.830 --> 01:03:43.350
I was like, well, I got something to offer you.
我说，好吧，我这儿倒是有样东西能给你。

1404
01:03:43.590 --> 01:03:44.590
I mean, I got scars.
我是说，我有伤疤。

1405
01:03:44.690 --> 01:03:47.110
I got scars all the live long day.
我身上到处都是伤疤。

1406
01:03:47.350 --> 01:03:48.970
I was like, you like scars?
我就问，你喜欢伤疤？

1407
01:03:49.170 --> 01:03:51.110
And she was like, yeah, I love scars.
她说，对啊，我超爱伤疤。

1408
01:03:51.310 --> 01:03:53.510
And I was like, oh, my gosh.
当时我心想，天哪。

1409
01:03:54.170 --> 01:03:57.410
And so I have this, you know, a fling.
于是我们就有了那段，你知道，露水情缘。

1410
01:03:57.590 --> 01:04:00.250
I don't even know what it was that was going on between us.
我甚至都不知道我们之间到底算什么。

1411
01:04:00.350 --> 01:04:02.750
But she had the, it's a Rolex watch.
但她当时戴着，那是块劳力士手表。

1412
01:04:02.910 --> 01:04:05.930
And for whatever, oh, we had exchanged watches.
不管怎么说，哦，我们交换了手表。

1413
01:04:06.110 --> 01:04:06.770
She had a Rolex.
她有一块劳力士。

1414
01:04:07.050 --> 01:04:08.590
I had a Timex.
我有一块天美时。

1415
01:04:08.810 --> 01:04:11.890
And just one of those little plastic digital watches.
就是那种普通的塑料电子表。

1416
01:04:12.330 --> 01:04:18.810
And so we exchanged watches while we were having our fling or whatever was going on.
所以我们在那段露水情缘或者说不清是什么的关系里，交换了手表。

1417
01:04:18.810 --> 01:04:23.910
And then when we, when it ended, I went to give her her watch back.
后来当这段关系结束时，我去把表还给她。

1418
01:04:23.910 --> 01:04:26.210
And she said, I want you to keep that.
她说，我想让你留着它。

1419
01:04:26.390 --> 01:04:30.970
And I was like, oh, I can't keep your Rolex.
我说，噢，我不能收你的劳力士。

1420
01:04:31.590 --> 01:04:34.150
And she was like, I want you to have it.
她说，我就是想让你留着。

1421
01:04:34.430 --> 01:04:35.990
And I was like, wow.
我说，哇。

1422
01:04:36.270 --> 01:04:39.450
And so I walked away with a Rolex.
就这样，我带着一块劳力士离开了。

1423
01:04:40.050 --> 01:04:40.610
Wow.
哇。

1424
01:04:40.890 --> 01:04:41.090
Yeah.
是啊。

1425
01:04:41.550 --> 01:04:43.470
That is an amazing story.
这故事太棒了。

1426
01:04:43.950 --> 01:04:45.890
And she does like scars.
而且她确实喜欢伤疤。

1427
01:04:46.130 --> 01:04:47.530
I will confirm.
我可以证实这一点。

1428
01:04:47.530 --> 01:04:49.330
She's really into scars.
她真的很迷伤疤。

1429
01:04:49.590 --> 01:04:56.370
You got the gift of this person being completely, truly like turned on and attracted to you.
你得到了一份礼物，这个人完全、真心实意地被你吸引，为你着迷。

1430
01:04:56.530 --> 01:04:56.650
Yeah.
没错。

1431
01:04:56.810 --> 01:04:59.750
In this new form that you were so insecure about.
还是以你曾经感到非常自卑的那种外在形式。

1432
01:05:00.170 --> 01:05:01.790
And you got a luxury watch.
而且你还得到了一块名表。

1433
01:05:01.950 --> 01:05:02.430
Yes, I did.
没错，确实。

1434
01:05:02.470 --> 01:05:03.290
Out of this relationship.
从这段关系里得到的。

1435
01:05:03.570 --> 01:05:03.750
I am not.
我不是那种人。

1436
01:05:03.750 --> 01:05:05.170
I don't think it gets better than that.
我觉得没有比这更好的事了。

1437
01:05:05.270 --> 01:05:05.610
No.
确实。

1438
01:05:05.810 --> 01:05:12.210
And I am not somebody that, I'm just, I never would have bought a Rolex.
